  ExpressionUUID->"7572137d-0cfa-7646-ac6a-bb5ac0fe52da"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a692fab6-f517-ca4b-8f79-7a5ac512a4ef"],

Cell["Special arrays", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"981e32b5-7774-d24b-8c0b-17100d04bd75"],

Cell["\<\
Constant arrays and the generalized Kronecker deltas, in any order, dimension \
and value domain. Each declares the strongest symmetry that actually holds of \
it.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0199d5ad-ecf6-6d47-85a4-b0965302cf38"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["ZeroArray", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "34241514-ae69-e947-ab0e-d5225d99e4d8"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "every entry zero"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7c5f7b88-bbe2-ba45-baa8-950f5f2ffe3a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["OneArray", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "da15437b-267e-a248-8406-2199b680c924"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "every entry one"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"99d4878a-ab7b-f54d-99a8-4e9afc3187f0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["IdentityArray", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "e9814374-8444-0943-a35f-e505c3141874"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "one where all the indices agree, zero elsewhere"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"86a96064-106e-8240-8ba9-899fe12d56ba"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["PartialIdentityArray", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"61b40ae0-62a3-7f46-af8b-3819a3b3e508"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "one where the indices at chosen positions agree"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2bae8308-ebbc-924a-ab7f-705df691883d"],

Cell["Contraction", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"b74da89b-c892-e944-996f-ac253974c5bb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["ArrayMultiply", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "9500b7a4-4725-5346-9025-14720b9b2115"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "contract arrays by an index specification, in the manner of Einstein \
summation"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"409be682-3489-1241-8b89-58c48288633b"],

Cell["\<\
The specification is written either as a string, \"ij,jk->ik\", or as a rule \
between lists of index labels. An index may occur in any number of the arrays \
and in the output as well, so diagonals and three-way contractions are \
expressible, not only pairwise ones. A 0-array is named by an empty group of \
labels, and contracting every index away gives one back.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4d4a163b-28d7-d542-957f-c6a34a000eb8"],

Cell["Drawing arrays", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"17ed4891-1b6e-6e4d-93a8-2301f03efcab"],

Cell["\<\
There are two families, and an array of any order may be drawn in either. The \
flat family gives plane pictures throughout: a row of cells at order one, a \
grid at order two, and above that a nesting of those, a grid whose cells hold \
grids. The spatial family gives cubes arranged in space throughout: a line of \
cubes, a plane of them, a lattice, and above that the same lattices tiled \
through space, block beside block, all in one picture.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"037bb4c8-5d46-714a-ae6b-e30144b00c2d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Which indices go outside and which inside is a choice rather than a fact \
about the array, and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\"\<Nesting\>\"", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "e81f69fa-7656-d047-ba44-e1f7dc62d5c3"],
 " makes it. A flat picture holds one or two indices at a time and a spatial \
one holds three, so that is the only difference between the two defaults."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4f99e332-7b8a-354e-8e14-37ec9923d6c9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["ArrayGraphics", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "937d3fb9-d69b-4742-b7ce-d01c2e76f718"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "draw an array of any order in the plane"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9e584d25-5fb5-b74b-8776-15c4a956e298"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["ArrayGraphics3D", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "9f288c35-8cb5-7444-9049-7b660215de0d"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "draw an array of any order as cubes in space"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e4c93a58-9b87-8248-9d20-6db507e08bfb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["ArrayNesting", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "dd4800be-f064-cf44-9bc8-da7d006bbf0d"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "how the indices are split by default, for either family"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d77c9f5a-98d4-244a-9cc0-10284d4caa52"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["HypermatrixGraphics", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"8d8b29b6-7fce-da4b-b63f-2ea1e5f670ad"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "draw every array of a hypermatrix, in the plane"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4fe10fce-88e9-db41-9faa-2769999ab823"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["HypermatrixGraphics3D", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"688edfac-c65f-3c47-bd71-5b204f17e4b2"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the same, as cubes in space"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"aee2e88c-c177-2b4c-8913-2eab79d08b6f"],

Cell["Adding and multiplying entry by entry", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"e8c49119-3d36-4b47-a318-fc89c31cf458"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["ArrayAdd", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "a629d3ed-c78d-2641-9ac1-e75ea2becb8b"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "add arrays entry by entry"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"36bf6602-5862-8e4a-a6d2-bb6e85ee1936"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["ArrayTimes", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "6e7af2f2-c5f7-5a4c-87f3-30a944be8371"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "multiply arrays entry by entry"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6bb2cc05-b35e-8546-a78c-18d16961e8df"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "These are the multilinear structure of arrays, as against the contraction \
ArrayMultiply. Arrays of the same dimensions combine entry by entry, and a \
0-array, having no shape of its own, reaches every entry \[LongDash] which is \
why scalar multiplication needs no name of its own. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Plus", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "1667e620-bc5b-524b-ac5a-b3e4100cfe8e"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Times", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "e2e10675-124d-ee42-be38-b10c3ae97d8d"],
 " on array objects are the same operations, so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"2", " ", "a"}], " ", "+", " ", "b"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"66ab86fc-9bdf-b14d-8761-0f227a3e3222"],
 " means what it looks like."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a95e54a2-3407-0245-98f0-0e3a12aa2337"],

Cell["Equational identities", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"9b4b8b47-2c22-a94e-b543-738d2d9231bf"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["FindArrayEquations", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"01206cb8-bf3b-ff41-92c7-1a58ba27e731"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "search for equations between all nestings of given operations over given \
arguments"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0571edae-212e-454d-8d94-a8c783f2a173"],

Cell["\<\
The search screens candidates on random numerical arrays first, which is \
fast, and verifies only the survivors on symbolic arrays. Matrix \
multiplication on three arguments returns associativity; the Fish product on \
five returns a twisted ternary associativity; the Bhattacharya-Mesner product \
on five returns nothing. An operation of arity one may be nested, so that the \
involutivity of a transpose is within reach, and an equation that follows \
from the others is not reported.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2c56ac25-d437-324e-b147-ec68c95c09a7"],

Cell["From hypergraphs to hypermatrices", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"628f7c64-9bcc-674c-8a2b-b48ace94f95f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The two halves of the package meet here. An edge has an arity and a \
symmetry type; an array has an order and a symmetry; and the two vocabularies \
line up one for one \[LongDash] ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\"\<Directed\>\"", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "b93e1a2e-a955-5f41-86a9-8a3dac96c2a6"],
 " with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\"\<Rigid\>\"", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "221055dd-1882-2346-80dd-bccbfc093187"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\"\<Cyclic\>\"", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "5b87e4ef-3da1-344e-86e9-fb6028fde44b"],
 " with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\"\<Cyclic\>\"", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "898de833-dbec-894e-b210-2fc82cc3cdfc"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\"\<Unordered\>\"", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"83509aa6-b6d4-d94d-9182-8294aa2bf0fb"],
 " with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\"\<Symmetric\>\"", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"d2383268-0963-7f44-9f52-8e7c22f4a677"],
 ". An array holds one symmetry and one order, so the edges are gathered by \
arity and symmetry type together and each group becomes one array."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4524a4f8-2b56-c14d-b4ea-9f640b4786c5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["AdjacencyHypermatrix", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"383556ea-bfed-484b-888b-e5fece9b5ab0"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the adjacency hypermatrix of a hypergraph"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4fa345e1-57d3-8947-9128-50d8b7fd2b13"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Identical copies of an edge share an entry, so a repeated edge comes out as \
an integer multiple. With ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"\"\<Labeled\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"b15ff8fd-1b42-2945-aa09-dcdcfecd38de"],
 " the entries are the edge labels themselves rather than counts, which needs \
the hypergraph to be simple \[LongDash] one entry cannot hold two labels."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"16906e73-a354-5c4b-892e-61fc13c2f907"],

Cell["\<\
The entry at an index tuple counts the edges sitting on it, and every tuple \
of an orbit reads the same count, which is what makes each array carry its \
symmetry by construction. Nothing is lost in the passage: the canonical \
entries name exactly the edges that went in.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b8b7d450-a8c3-3b4a-a315-21b49a884366"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The vertices are a set, so numbering the indices is a choice; the \
Hypergraph constructor makes it by storing its vertices sorted. That is \
deterministic but not invariant \[LongDash] renaming the vertices can permute \
the indices \[LongDash] so for an invariant of the isomorphism class, compose \
with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["CanonicalHypergraph", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"f6b89735-de0a-ae42-b880-29e70239db75"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1fd9b47a-6031-4a44-a785-94c961ac6434"],

Cell["Hypermatrices", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"20a8162c-a960-0a4b-8e23-0d85c36ab5fc"],

Cell["\<\
A hypermatrix is a list of arrays held in canonical order: lowest order \
first, then the shorter dimensions, then symmetry taking symmetric before \
cyclic before rigid. Giving the same arrays in a different order produces the \
identical expression.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"14be2058-ee0b-1846-be32-8c968826706f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Hypermatrix", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "e253ae4b-5211-5642-b0f7-e3736ea4fc71"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "a canonically ordered list of arrays"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d4ec38b6-b8c8-414d-960c-657bfa433723"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["HypermatrixArrays", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"70f4cf82-9f19-1a4c-8baa-d9964f4a8773"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the arrays, in canonical order"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9d45434d-7760-9342-b7a9-b0833bfcea89"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["HypermatrixQ", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "af0218ae-1c2c-af4c-a8ca-6c8bdb3e628a"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "test for a valid hypermatrix object"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"32b15d4b-a032-8c41-aef3-fa6213e05990"],

Cell["Messages", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"c59b1038-9ad8-f041-9167-827a17e28833"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"Edge", "::", "sym"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"2732562b-cd56-ee4b-a487-86011dfb33c6"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the given edge symmetry type is not one of the three recognized ones"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ebf96d8d-6b3d-e649-95d0-8468c76704f9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"Edge", "::", "spec"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"ffaa2e39-c1b6-354c-8c28-68fc4069d352"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the expression is not a valid hyperedge specification"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3d0ff4e5-8ea0-834f-a969-9803f5c19311"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"Hypergraph", "::", "spec"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"b3a72293-5089-604f-9c4e-c6a2d918c54c"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the expression is not a valid hypergraph specification"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"36cb06f8-0129-4941-8e1b-e8e9378ba77d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"Hypergraph", "::", "vlbl"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"981695b9-3029-7f44-91aa-dcf77d34484b"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "one vertex identifier was given more than one label"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9d17e362-9081-0845-bd55-45f6c84c4351"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"CanonicalHypergraph", "::", "large"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"eb393aaa-bbec-6a4e-bb54-3cd569ef01dd"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the isomorphism search will be slow at this size"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e643df72-118c-ee46-8364-231a99528edb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayObject", "::", "nosym"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"ebcc581d-e012-d047-8896-c51fed0eb982"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the entries are not invariant under the declared symmetry"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"29169a19-c7d0-8448-9a88-492200050afb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayObject", "::", "irreg"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"f2884543-f03b-b344-936e-f2acc01b44b1"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "an irregular array cannot carry a symmetry"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"203e8bf8-9ada-fb4c-900f-2dd0165eb38b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayObject", "::", "data"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"b7523f44-8106-fb44-98f5-fda672d03ae5"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the entries are not a rectangular array"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7da6741d-f3b3-a24c-b88c-cb5495be7012"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"GenerateSymbolicArray", "::", "name"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"b56e682c-3194-c94c-a2c6-081e25bb48ea"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "an array name must be a symbol or a string"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"73f0b2d3-2686-0a4f-b213-6cf5d1e131c1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"Hypermatrix", "::", "arrays"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"bc959356-c48f-d14d-a140-bc7284cc0f3d"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "something given was not an array"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"52dcef9a-f8c5-5f49-8933-405751fb7a29"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayMultiply", "::", "rank"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"2323c65f-c1fa-544a-bf9f-f46ba12be556"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "an array has a different number of indices from its specification"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d48d6131-63ae-fe4f-9644-3c3870147c49"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayMultiply", "::", "dims"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"fd2a9843-dc4e-4c4f-a3b5-135a3d495459"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "one index label is used with two different lengths"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9bd76085-db43-6441-94bf-e2b97698c580"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayMultiply", "::", "out"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"0364c078-203d-3d44-960d-d2dc472d7aad"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "an output index does not occur among the inputs"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b9b147bc-1b33-4d42-9f06-77c30574c7e1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"FindArrayEquations", "::", "arity"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"b85c3e88-fb84-574b-b380-2151d33b3640"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the arity of an operation could not be determined"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"bc81de19-9178-5b48-8794-8d0c69cda6ed"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"FindArrayEquations", "::", "eval"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"594e818e-75dd-1840-a534-4e1b04bf4982"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "no nesting evaluated on arrays of the shape used"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b3da4cb3-9a73-eb4a-a31b-f109546b89bd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"FindArrayEquations", "::", "shape"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"af150556-a8bd-0044-a03c-9db0c8a85103"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "no order from 1 to 5 suits every operation"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2e85b715-d19c-4b41-85a9-a05997c29fba"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"FindArrayEquations", "::", "depth"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"1ba320ff-2525-b54c-95e0-719031878157"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "\"UnaryDepth\" is not a non-negative integer"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"66032b04-5b27-064d-a6d6-93a477da1db8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayAdd", "::", "dims"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"119df918-0506-df47-935e-f36e0f2b01d6"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the arrays are not of the same dimensions"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3843cd2d-435b-6b44-82ae-b354d4f88118"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayTimes", "::", "dims"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"b4f9f2ce-c141-f44c-8fd1-ec8cb4080191"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the same, for multiplication entry by entry"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"df0ed029-53c1-b043-8d92-bd8d46ec1e61"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayGraphics", "::", "nesting"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"0d610ce6-1d46-5e46-bd0f-c21f2a2123f2"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the given nesting does not account for every index"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"10fdb1a7-c376-b642-8862-7aa5a00d70ef"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayGraphics", "::", "block"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"e544d7f1-6420-5548-98f8-2c71600cb481"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "a block of more than two indices has no flat picture"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"34cbd955-832b-a744-925e-9d5c15adb618"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayGraphics3D", "::", "block"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"8993587e-b784-5f4d-9468-ecdf88ce1c9b"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "a block of more than three indices has nowhere to go in space"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6859233a-ffd3-384f-9b72-e4a495c47e6a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"AdjacencyHypermatrix", "::", "hg"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"0e8795d8-6f33-f54e-8e53-54c76943ba41"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the argument is not a hypergraph"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3759a5de-1699-b640-9818-21d45963af75"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"HypergraphRule", "::", "hg"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"40c3608c-ed0b-9f42-aac1-cbf9f915f1e6"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "a side of a rule is not a hypergraph"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8803b1e4-7650-1644-a061-8eefd98cdde7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"HypergraphRuleApply", "::", "rule"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"f4455e62-3ad7-7549-b530-8a19553a6f94"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "what was given is not a rewrite rule"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c5ed656b-c48a-154f-bb7b-cfd10db6677f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"AdjacencyHypermatrix", "::", "nonsimple"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"04948fb5-abd2-b34a-9a88-bc5c1301f2c4"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "labels cannot be entries unless no edge is repeated"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"caee4597-4bb1-b249-b5f0-8eff8ef49ef7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayGraphics", "::", "big"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"b000bff6-d491-d142-a025-f1e76965bfc9"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the array has too many entries to be drawn legibly"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f3c9d86b-98b3-9a4c-8233-f62329ca9df0"],

Cell["Rewriting", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"d76755ea-6f54-2e4c-9731-092cca7cdb7d"],

Cell["\<\
A rewrite rule is a pair of hypergraphs. Applying it means finding the ways \
its input sits inside a hypergraph, and for each of them replacing what was \
matched by the output. Each such way is an event, reported as an association \
saying not only what the new hypergraph is but what was matched, what was \
created and what was destroyed.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6362769e-6364-9341-b12f-263f8a4b209c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["HypergraphRule", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "dafcb4de-5937-8c4e-961d-eede9fd90517"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "a rewrite rule, as a pair of hypergraphs"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"05cb0298-3643-a049-99d2-72453246541d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["HypergraphRuleQ", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "6f3c3693-60cd-fd44-a4fe-59cfb1c26b77"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "test for a valid rule"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4b8fa1da-bec2-564e-b116-09dcb9e2dfae"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["HypergraphRuleApply", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"658dc5a8-9b08-464f-938e-b2d877c44db2"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "apply a rule, giving one event per match; rule[hg] is the same"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1ca1f066-7b44-d041-a93b-be9b6794235f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["HypergraphRuleMatches", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"f3d0d6fa-8b74-fc48-aae3-0d6946b9734b"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the ways the input sits inside a hypergraph, without rewriting"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9590020e-631b-2149-b9ff-a29b212155c8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Symmetry types must agree between a pattern edge and the edge it lies on, \
and the pattern is matched over the orderings that symmetry allows. Labels \
constrain: a pattern carrying no label matches whatever it lies on, one \
carrying a label matches only the same label, and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"\"\<Labeled\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "False"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"53dc5330-9d29-144d-b541-a7898897bcac"],
 " ignores them. The shape of all this follows the reference paclet, so that \
rules written for that one read the same here."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7913b539-82ef-6243-bee9-327cae70f65c"],

Cell["Not yet implemented", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"a0c6a442-e191-ba46-976a-7564eb2868e5"],

Cell["\<\
The objects, isomorphism, the array algebra, the drawing, the adjacency \
hypermatrix and the core of rewriting are all in place. What remains of the \
rewriting is the machinery around it: the generations of states a rule \
produces, the causal graph of its events, and the conditions under which two \
events depend on one another or their matches overlap. After that come the \
plex diagrams that tie rewriting to hypermatrix algebra, and a visual editor \
for hypergraphs and for rules.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4317e386-9e9d-114b-9dc6-2f994afdd304"]
},
WindowSize->{820, 750},
FrontEndVersion->"15.0 for Microsoft Windows (64-bit) (July 2, 2026)",
StyleDefinitions->"Default.nb",
ExpressionUUID->"aae57b0f-c3fc-3c4c-9427-57379acf44b0"
]
